# SYNOPSIS

```usage
cp [-gux] fromfile tofile
cp [-x] fromfile ... todir
```

# DESCRIPTION

`cp` copies <fromfile> to <tofile>, or each <fromfile> into the directory <todir> under its last name.
A <tofile> that exists is cut to nothing and written; one that doesn't is made.
Directories aren't copied.

: `-x`
  Keep each file's time of last change.
: `-g`
  Accepted, for keeping the group.
: `-u`
  Accepted, for keeping the owner.

# SEE ALSO

mv(1), cat(1)

# DIAGNOSTICS

The exit string is `errors` if a file couldn't be copied, each one reported, such as `cp: a and b are the same file`, and `bad usage` for several files copied to what isn't a directory.

# BUGS

Files have no owners or groups, so `-g` and `-u` do nothing.
